 #uuid "c6ae7c04-0a9c-587c-af8d-7844f40ca12a" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435529 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435530 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435533 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435537 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435540 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1077 "selection" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435540 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435547 1079 #uuid "e1008d1e-ad25-59f1-8249-03f1bd3c30fe" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435526 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435531 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435541 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435542 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435543 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1077 "selection" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435531 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435548 1079 #uuid "f6aa0ef9-33dc-511a-a8b4-7535395d3236" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435549 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435545 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435549 1069 "q-129559" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435549 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435549 1071 "At which point on the surface $z={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-7$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector $v=⟨6,-8,-1⟩?$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435549 1072 #uuid "1863d48a-c899-5d14-89ee-82ba61f0f79b" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435549 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-7)=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-7)=4y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨2x,\\,4y,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨6,-8,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨2x,\\,4y,\\,-1⟩=⟨6,-8,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2cx=6 \\\\ 4cy=-8 \\\\ -c=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2(1)x=6\\,⟹\\,x=3.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n4(1)y=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=3$ and $y=-2$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & ={3}^{2}+2(-2)^{2}-7 \\\\  & =9+8-7 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(3,-2,10).$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435550 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435544 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435550 1069 "q-129477" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435550 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435550 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=x+y-{z}^{2}$ at the point $(1,0,1,0).$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435550 1072 #uuid "6b798538-8660-5c1f-9d93-5bdad8bdb40c" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435550 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y-{z}^{2})=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y-{z}^{2})=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x+y-{z}^{2})=-2z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,0,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,0,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,0,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,0,1) & =-2(1)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-0 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,0,1)+(y-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,0,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,0,1) \\\\ w & =(x-1)+y-2(z-1) \\\\ w & =x+y-2z+1 \\\\ x+y-2z-w+1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435551 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435548 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435551 1069 "q-73849" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435551 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435551 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=2x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}z$ at the point $(2,-2,1,2).$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435551 1072 #uuid "923d3b9b-11dc-5749-a7e2-257ace8090ef" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435551 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}z)=2{y}^{2}-6xz \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}z)=4xy+{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}z)=2yz-3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(2,-2,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,-2,1) & =2(-2)^{2}-6(2)(1)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,-2,1) & =4(2)(-2)+(1)^{2}=-15 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,-2,1) & =2(-2)(1)-3(2)^{2}=-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-2 & =(x-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,-2,1)+(y+2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,-2,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,-2,1) \\\\ w-2 & =-4(x-2)-15(y+2)-16(z-1) \\\\ w-2 & =-4x+8-15y-30-16z+16 \\\\ 4x+15y+16z+w+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435552 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435546 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435552 1069 "q-73840" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435552 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435552 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)}$ at the point $(0,0,1).$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435552 1072 #uuid "986c989d-58b2-593e-8458-dc3fb233ef93" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435552 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)}) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)}) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(0,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,0) & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+0)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+0)=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,0) & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+0)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+0)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & =(x-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,0)+(y-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,0) \\\\ z-1 & =1(x-0)+1(y-0) \\\\ z-1 & =x+y \\\\ -x-y+z-1 & =0 \\\\ x+y-z+1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435553 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435547 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435553 1069 "q-129560" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435553 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435553 1071 "At which point on the surface $z=4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector $v=⟨-2,-5,1⟩?$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435553 1072 #uuid "e0b70f07-48f3-5e91-bb4d-83ea4566f9c8" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435553 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2})=-4x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2})=-10y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨-4x,\\,-10y,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨-2,-5,1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨-4x,\\,-10y,\\,-1⟩=⟨-2,-5,1⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-4cx=-2 \\\\ -10cy=-5 \\\\ -c=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-4(-1)x=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=-1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n-10(-1)y=-5\\,⟹\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =4-2{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-5{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{9}{4}).$" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435554 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435556 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435554 1062 #uuid "0af89c86-dd82-51d3-8a60-9428fdaf17c3" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435554 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435551 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435555 1062 #uuid "52566cd2-c610-5b7e-a93b-8dfb407f2200" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435555 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435553 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435556 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435557 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435556 1062 #uuid "8189ee1b-e555-5395-af62-45720087b2f5" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435556 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435550 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435557 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435555 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435557 1062 #uuid "9be88cd8-1668-517f-a1dd-283be301d1d2" 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435557 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435549 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435558 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435554 13194139534770 17592186045417 true] [17592186435558 1062 #uu